      "category": "List-item",
      "text": "1. Upon determining that a contract for professional services is required to supplement the work of agency staff, an agency should prepare an RFP setting forth the services to be performed and any pertinent information relative to them such as time limit, professional qualifications, etc. The agency should then circulate the RFP to at least three qualified firms to obtain their proposals as to the scope, cost, and time to perform the desired services. A useful guide to follow in the preparation and issuance",
